<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<resources>

    <!--
        Workaround for a crash at startup, not styling.

        MAUI's Android theme points bottomNavigationViewStyle at Widget.Design.BottomNavigationView,
        a style from the old Design library. Material Components 1.12 runs NavigationBarView through
        ThemeEnforcement, which rejects that style for not carrying a valid TextAppearance, so Shell
        throws in ShellItemRenderer.OnCreateView before a single page is shown:

            java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: This component requires that you specify a valid
            TextAppearance attribute. Update your app theme to inherit from Theme.MaterialComponents

        Overriding the style by name is enough: application resources win over the ones merged in
        from libraries, so the theme keeps pointing at this name and now resolves to the Material
        Components style. The theme itself is left alone - redeclaring it would mean copying the
        thirteen items MAUI puts in Maui.MainTheme.Base, which would drift on the next update. The
        parent stays on the Material 2 family because the app theme is Theme.MaterialComponents.

        This lives in the sample. The library ships no Android resources at all.
    -->
    <style
        name="Widget.Design.BottomNavigationView"
        parent="Widget.MaterialComponents.BottomNavigationView" />

</resources>
